body:
Hi and thanks for this excellent work! 

I am plugging in a custom sensor sim service to alpasim, but have encountered a few problem with the lidar rendering interface.

**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**

Currently the sensorsim interface does not make it possible to distinguish between two different lidars of the same type (e.g. 2 different PANDAR128 lidars mounted at different locations with different settings). It also does not expose any `get_available_lidars` function.

**Describe the solution you'd like**

Add first-class support for lidar, similar to what is there for rgb. The minimal case would be a logical_id per unique lidar, regardless of type, and a  way to list available lidars. Since it's tricky to enumerate all possible lidar types, one could add a catch-all OTHER type or something like that.

**Describe alternatives you've considered**

Assuming a one-to-one mapping between lidar type and logical id, but this is quickly problematic for multi-lidar setups.

As hinted at above, a logical_id field would also serve as a temporary workaround for supporting additional lidar types, since the sensorsim service could keep track of the beam patterns internally, and alpasim only needs to request renderings from lidar X, not caring about the type. 

Ideally this would also be accompanied by 

```
service SensorsimService {
    ...
    rpc get_available_lidars (AvailableLidarsRequest) returns (AvailableLidarReturn);
}
message AvailableLidarsRequest {
    string scene_id = 1;
}

enum LidarDeviceType {
    PANDAR128 = 0;
    AT128 = 1;
    // Optional: any additional predefined types
    OTHER = 2;
}

message LidarSpec {
    LidarDeviceType lidar_type = 2;
    string logical_id = 3;
}

message AvailableLidarsReturn {
    message AvailableLidar {
        LidarSpec intrinsics = 1;
        common.Pose rig_to_lidar = 2;
        string logical_id = 3;
    }

    repeated AvailableLidar available_lidars = 1;
}
```

Looking forward to hearing your thoughts on the matter.

Cheers, 
Adam
